over the years series finales have  become more than just the end of the TV  show now they're bona fide cultural  phenomenon leaving fans talking for  years let's take a look at some of the  greatest vinyl episodes of all time and  fair warning  we plan to totally spoil the ending six  feet under  HBO six feet under blended quirky and  poignant elements as well as any series  in recent memory so it isn't surprising  that its finale was a little bit of both  fans of the Fisher family watched in  stunned silence as youngest sibling  Claire left California for a job in New  York as the deserts Airy flash past her  window we saw flashes of the future for  the rest of the main characters in  typical six feet under style we've got a  glimpse of what happens to the whole  Fisher family including how they all age  and die one by one if you're not crying  by the end of this one you're already  dead inside Star Trek The Next  Generation entitled all good things  the final Star Trek The Next Generation  episode marked the end of seven great  seasons of highly acclaimed television  the series frequently explored social  ethical and philosophical issues as the  crew probed the depths of space and the  finale was no exception  Captain Picard finds his mind jumping  through three points in the same  timeline forcing him to think outside of  the known laws of physics to solve the  anomaly forced upon him by the  omnipotent obnoxious being Q that are  the cure alike some are almost  respectable Picard manages to solve the  conundrum returning to a scene from the  series first episode and proving to Q  that humanity's potential is limitless  much to Q's surprise the show ends with  a love letter to fans as the captain  joins a poker game with the other crew  members for the first time I should be  bonus what I'm proud of a girl Breaking  Bad during its five-year run Breaking  Bad evolved from just another TV drama  into a cultural phenomenon when the  series finally drew to a close in 2013  fans eagerly anticipated an episode that  promised to  wrap up an epic saga of crime greed and  vengeance and the show absolutely  delivered Walt returns from hiding and  manages to secure his family's future  exact his revenge and saved jesse from  captivity before going down in a blaze  of glory the way the final scene played  out was a direct punch to the gut for  fans as bad fingers baby blue plays in  the background walt lovingly examines  the meth lab jesse was forced to work in  and even as the sirens approach in the  distance you wonder if he might make it  out alive after all until he collapses  to the ground succumbing to a bullet  wound Buffy the Vampire Slayer  out of just Whedon's many television  series Buffy the Vampire Slayer is  perhaps the most beloved generating  legions of fans who still obsess about  the show to this day for the finale  Whedon pitted the Scooby Gang against a  malevolent enemy in a battle that  required the characters to work together  in one last showdown in the depths below  Sunnydale high as you might expect from  a show that never shied away from  mortality not everyone makes it out  alive after the survivors flee from the  wreckage and the School Bus  dawn poses the question many fans were  asking as the credits rolled  yeah Murphy  what are we gonna do now Friday Night  Lights  MBC's high school football drama Friday  Night Lights was always more about the  cost of characters than the sport itself  appropriately enough when millions tuned  in to the finale  they were treated to an episode that  focused on the lives of the characters  long after the last pass was thrown and  the cheers of the crowd faded away with  the state championship in the past the  characters are shown in the future with  many storylines neatly wrapped up most  importantly Coach Taylor finally got to  move on building a new life for himself  with his wife in Philadelphia  [Music]  yells come  sons of anarchy from 2008 to 2014 sons  of anarchy 